            <ArticleTitle>Wiktor coronary stent.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>665-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Wiktor stent is a unique balloon-expandable tantalum coil stent currently undergoing clinical trials to determine the efficacy and safety of the device for reducing restenosis and for salvaging a failed angioplasty (bailout). This article discusses the stent in detail, the procedure, possible complications, and its advantages and disadvantages.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
